  <div class="practitioners">
    <div class="practitioner-card">
      <img src="/img/Jsq.jpg" alt="Jenny" class="practitioner-photo">
      <div class="practitioner-name">Jenny</div>
      <div class="practitioner-role">Yoga & Sound Healing</div>
      <p class="practitioner-bio">Jenny is a Registered Yoga Teacher (RYT) with Yoga Alliance, bringing over a decade of dedicated experience in yoga practice and teaching. She has guided a diverse range of students and has been actively involved in leading and contributing to numerous 200-hour and 500-hour Yoga Teacher Training programmes, mentoring and supporting the next generation of yoga teachers. In recent years she has expanded her practice into Sound Healing, completing extensive training in therapeutic sound, breathwork and meditation. Known for her calm presence and authentic approach, these skills inform every class she teaches and every joint session she delivers alongside Seb.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="practitioner-card">
      <img src="/img/Ssq.jpg" alt="Seb" class="practitioner-photo">
      <div class="practitioner-name">Seb</div>
      <div class="practitioner-role">Qigong</div>
      <p class="practitioner-bio">Seb brings over two decades of training in Asian healing arts. He has practised Yoga since 1997, studying with masters in Japan and India, and is a certified Yoga teacher through IYF Asia, qualified in South Korea. Since 2010 he has trained extensively in authentic Qigong, studying and practising with masters across Mainland China, Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand and Scotland. He is also a certified Therapeutic Thai bodywork therapist and instructor, accredited by TTMA Japan since 2018. His deep understanding of Qi cultivation, the principles of Traditional Chinese Medicine as they relate to energy work, and hands-on therapeutic bodywork informs every class he teaches and every joint session he delivers alongside Jenny.</p>
    </div>
